# Boot-Time Restore Implementation Plan

## Overview
This plan implements boot-time restore of session state for the GameRuntimeServer. The implementation will restore the simulation state, agent configurations, and thread connections when the server starts, allowing the game to resume from a previous session without requiring a full restart.

## Implementation Plan

### 1. Modify GameRuntimeServer.ts

#### A. Add restore logic to `restoreSession` method
Replace the current `restoreSession` implementation with the following:

```typescript
private async restoreSession(): Promise<void> {
  const saved = await this.stateStore.load();
  if (!saved) {
    return;
  }

  const content = this.contentStore.getContent();

  // Restore simulation state if available
  if (saved.simulation) {
    this.simulation = Simulation.fromState(saved.simulation, content);
    this.seed = saved.simulation.seed;

    // Restore agent configurations
    for (const agent of saved.simulation.agents ?? []) {
      this.agentConfigs.set(agent.id, { id: agent.id, name: agent.name });
    }

    // Restore agent loop state
    this.resetAgentLoopState((saved.simulation.agents ?? []).map((agent) => agent.id));
  } 
  // Fallback to single agent if no simulation state
  else if (typeof saved.seed === "number") {
    this.simulation = new Simulation(saved.seed, DEFAULT_WORLD_SIZE, DEFAULT_WORLD_SIZE, content, [
      { id: "agent-1", name: "Agent 1" }
    ]);
    this.seed = saved.seed;
    this.agentConfigs.set("agent-1", { id: "agent-1", name: "Agent 1" });
    this.resetAgentLoopState(["agent-1"]);
  } 
  else {
    return;
  }

  // Restore thread connections
  this.threadIds = { gameplayByAgentId: {} };
  this.threadToAgentId.clear();

  if (saved.threadIds?.gameplayByAgentId) {
    for (const [agentId, threadId] of Object.entries(saved.threadIds.gameplayByAgentId)) {
      this.threadIds.gameplayByAgentId[agentId] = threadId;
      this.threadToAgentId.set(threadId, agentId);
    }
  }

  if (saved.threadIds?.builder && saved.threadIds.builder) {
    this.threadIds.builder = saved.threadIds.builder;
  }

  // Restore metrics
  if (saved.metrics) {
    this.metrics.setSnapshot(saved.metrics);
  }

  // Set phase to running
  this.phase = "running";
  this.preparedSeed = null;

  // Send restored state to clients
  this.sendSessionState();
  this.sendWorldSnapshot();

  await this.logReplay("session.restored", {
    seed: this.seed,
    tick: this.simulation.getState().tick,
    threadIds: this.threadIds
  });
}
```

#### B. Update `startSession` to handle restore conflict
Add a check at the beginning of `startSession` to prevent conflicts with restored sessions:

```typescript
private async startSession(payload: SessionStartPayload): Promise<void> {
  // If we have a restored session, don't start a new one
  if (this.phase === "running" && this.simulation) {
    this.emitError("session_conflict", "Session already active. Use reset to start new session.", false);
    return;
  }

  // ... rest of startSession implementation
}
```

### 2. Update StateStore to handle simulation state

The current `StateStore` already supports `SessionSnapshot` which includes `SimulationState`, so no changes are needed to `stateStore.ts`.

